From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 22:47:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lophinya: exp - Region-local parallel phase framework
 skeleton (DEC-69)

RegionParallelPhase<E,S,R>: snapshot (owner thread) / compute (worker thread,
no live-state access) / commit (owner thread, only after re-validation).

RegionParallelRunner: server-wide shared bounded worker pool (not per-region -
would starve regions on a small box), bounded queue with immediate synchronous
fallback on rejection (never blocks), hard-deadline barrier wait (region tick
thread must never block indefinitely - see the folia-economy-harness incident
in SESSION_HANDOFF.md 8), and per-result re-validation (alive, not removed,
still owned by the calling region) immediately before commit - this single
check is what makes region merge/split, entity unload, and shutdown safe
without special-case code for any of them.

SensorShadowPhase: the first (no-op) phase, wired into Brain#tick in the
lophine-server/src/minecraft/java worktree (see that repo's matching exp/
branch) to measure the framework's own overhead before any real AI sub-phase
is attached.

Design doc: project-docs/evidence/20260805-region-parallel-phase-framework-
design.md. Authorization: DECISIONS.md DEC-69 (CORE-SHIM-RESEARCH scope only -
exp/* isolated prototyping, not authorization to merge into ver/26.2-nya).

exp/* isolated exploration branch. Not for merge into ver/26.2-nya.

